code measured per specs/HARNESS.md — and those three must stay explicitly blocked rather than silently green.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce at the tip, from the repository root: the row's probe prints `unchanged_rows=0 dispatch_targets_refs=0 root_gate_refs=0 manifest_check_refs=0` then `ABSENT: four PRD verification cells name artifacts no shipped test provides`, and exits 0. Once an arm exists for any of those four cells, the corresponding counter is non-zero and the second line reads `PRESENT:`.\n2. Each of CF-101, CF-103, CF-104, CF-106, CF-107, CF-108 and CF-111 gains a tests/ arm that can FAIL when its requirement is violated, and docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md's cell for that requirement names the selftest section that proves it. A green arm that cannot go red is not acceptance (AGENTS.md rule 2).\n3. CF-103's arm runs two `--apply` passes in one fixed `$HOME` and fails when the second run rewrites `node.json` (its `created_at` differs); the red arm is kept in the gate and recorded in an evidence artifact.\n4. CF-104's arm fails on uid 0 and on a `sudo`/`apt` invocation injected into the ladder transcript; the red arm is kept and recorded.\n5. CF-111's arm asserts all ten manifest fields of `specs/NODE.md` by name and fails naming each absent key; the red arm drops a field and the arm prints a FAIL row naming it.\n6. Three requirements stay explicitly blocked rather than silently green: CF-110 (no destroy path ships — CF-008), CF-112 (no `dispatch-targets` consumer ships) and CF-106 (`opencode` unmeasured per `specs/HARNESS.md`) may not be marked PASS by a commit that does not ship the missing code.\n7. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` with 0 FAIL rows and keeps every existing PASS row; `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK`.\n8. The commit carries a `ch:trace` marker naming row CF-083, the sections added and the evidence artifact, and its message states AGENTS.md rule 2 (every check must be able to fail).","probe":"u=$(grep -rn 